---
import BaseLayout from '~/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE, href } from '~/lib/site';
const body='### Server name and maker\n\n### Repository or official documentation\n\n### The workflow it helps with\n\n### Installation, authentication and permissions\n\n### Limitations and maintenance status\n\n### Your relationship to the server\n';
const suggestion=SITE.repo+'/issues/new?title='+encodeURIComponent('Server suggestion: ')+'&body='+encodeURIComponent(body);
---
<BaseLayout title="Suggest a server" description="Suggest an MCP server for editorial consideration. Share its source, practical use and limitations."><section class="container page-head" style="padding-block:72px 40px"><p class="kicker">For makers and practitioners</p><h1 class="t-h1">Show us the useful part.</h1><p class="t-lead" style="margin-top:24px;max-width:54ch">A focused tool with a clear job is a good starting point. Tell us what it does and where it fits.</p></section><section class="container"><div class="prose-wrap prose"><h2>What to include</h2><ol><li>The server's name, maker and official source.</li><li>One concrete workflow it helps with.</li><li>Setup instructions, required accounts and permissions.</li><li>Known limitations and current maintenance status.</li><li>Your relationship to the project.</li></ol><p>Suggestions open as public GitHub issues and require a GitHub account. Include only information you are comfortable publishing. Keep credentials and private customer data out of the issue.</p><p>Editorial review is selective. Submission does not guarantee inclusion, and paid placements are not currently offered.</p><p><a class="btn btn-primary" href={suggestion} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open a suggestion on GitHub ↗</a></p><p><a href={href('/standards')}>Read the listing standards</a>. For a correction, <a href={SITE.repo+'/issues/new'}>open an issue</a> and link the listing and supporting source.</p></div></section></BaseLayout>
